<title>SINGAPORE: Shareholder cuts Lion Teck Chiang stake.</title>
<headline>Shareholder cuts Lion Teck Chiang stake.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lion Teck Chiang Ltd (LTC) said on Thursday a major shareholder, Andalas Development Sdn Bhd, had sold 9.36 percent or 13.29 million LTC shares at Singapore $1.30 each.</p>
<p>After the sale, Andalas's LTC stake has been reduced to 3.49 percent from 13.72 percent previously, LTC said in a statement.</p>
<p>The property and steel company said Andalas had sold 8.59 million shares through a public offer on April 16 and a further 4.7 million was sold to Bidara Holdings Sdn Bhd on April 17.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
